 "note": [
  "Scripture came from the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, irvhin), fetched whole from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx) — all 66 books, 31,104 verses on disk, so translators looked verses up rather than working from a citation-only crib.",
  "A `mined` row is an exact byte substring of the IRV of at least 45 characters, measured against the finished chapter — not a translator's claim. A verse whose person, number or wording the translator bent to fit the author's argument is recorded self_rendered even where a long verbatim span survives.",
  "This book was translated by several agents working different chapter ranges in parallel, then reconciled: conventions were settled by measuring the shipped hi corpus and the IRV rather than by majority vote among the ranges. An orthography sweep normalised anusvara to conjunct forms, protecting every word form the IRV itself spells with anusvara so pasted verses keep the Bible's own spelling."
 ],
